{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/12818-scion-2e-mechanical-balance","id":12818,"title":"Scion 2e mechanical balance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-17T11:10:43-08:00","id":12818,"title":"Scion 2e mechanical balance","content":"So, I am curious to know if the folks working on 2e have taken a look at the math on rolling multiple dice against a fixed target number to receive a fixed target number of successes. there are quite a few examples of this in the system (combat comes to mind). The bits that I've done shows a pretty big cliff once you reach a certain ratio of dice/difficulty.<br /> <br /> My own experience with it has shown that it is exceptionally difficult for a GM to balance these between characters, leading to very tight ranges (3 or less dice in pool size) of ability that work in a way that might seem reasonable. Anything that hits those pool sizes has an extremely large effect one way or the other (assuring success or failure).<br /> <br /> I think I'd really like to see something a little more linear and predictable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T11:40:58-08:00","id":12838,"title":"","content":"Math is actually a Big Thing in my book.<br /> <br /> Actually, right now we're investigating the matter a bit, and working the math around various target numbers. Care to expound on your thoughts a bit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T11:43:28-08:00","id":12842,"title":"","content":"Rolling d10, seeing if it is a 7-9 to acquire 1 success or a 10 to acquire 2 successes, means that on average you get 1 success for every 2 dice you roll, but your change of not rolling a success on a given dice is 60%. Which is neat, given that you should only roll for things that might actually fail.<br /> <br /> The problem with this system is that many dice on a single roll mostly means that you'll get half that amount of successes, which is linear. And automatic success that exceed the dice pool make the rolling mostly pointless, which is fine from a narrative standpoint.<br /> <br /> One cool system that I found was rolling a pool of dice and counting pairs. Like roll 5d10: 5 3 3 7 7 would mean that you got 1 pair of 3 and 1 pair of 7, which in fact gives the player 2 results instead of 1 (the usual number of successes). This cold mean that on combat the attack stroke at hit boxes number 3 and 7 once, or the character performed an attack on the timer 7, then something might have happened before the character's second attack on timer 3. Many things may use this method to see how well and how fast a given action was performed. The problem is that at 2 dice you have 10% chance of a pair, 3 dice 28% of a pair, 4 dice 49.6% of a pair, 5 dice 69.76% of a pair,... and only goes up and beyond 100% if you roll more than 10 dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":384,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","user":"Man in Black","date":". 11-17-2013, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T14:02:03-08:00","id":12942,"title":"","content":"It's not as big of a cliff as you think, if you keep in mind the golden rule: <b>use enemies at multiple levels of difficulty.</b><br /> <br /> Almost every single fight should have at least two tiers of difficulty. One so your heavy weight combat characters can shine against, and one so your middle weight combat characters can shine against. Your light weights are probably not even involved in the combat, or are throwing around social/mental powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T14:14:29-08:00","id":12948,"title":"","content":"My biggest problem has been in a group with a non-frontliner (no str, no dex, some sta), a big tank (str, sta, no dex), and a dex monkey (no str, moderate sta, a lot of dex).<br /> <br /> When you put in something that will challenge a non-frontliner, it has very little chance of affecting the other guys. Not like &quot;10%&quot;, like 0.1%. On the other hand, you have something that can impact the dex guy, it will obliterate the non-frontliner. He can't take the damage spill over from the extra successes. <br /> <br /> I did up an anydice to help show the radical drop - <a href=\"http://anydice.com/program/2dd7\" target=\"_blank\">http://anydice.com/program/2dd7</a><br /> <br /> Essentially, you put in a 15 dice guy that can hit the dex monkey at 33% (lets say he's got a defense of 9), it's hitting your non-frontliner with a defense of 4 nearly 100%of the time, and getting extra damage dice 87% of the time. He's getting _five_ extra dice 33% of the time. Dang near enough to kill him, even if he has some soak.<br /> <br /> so now you are forced into an arms race where you now must compete on Dex (or whatever thing it is)<br /> <br /> Then you toss in the triangular scaling (factorial, but additive) of epic successes and you start having shifts between levels of epic stats that are bigger than the entire drop in the curve... meaning that you have +1 epic stat over a guy, and poof, no chance at all, not even with rolling. Add in things like Untouchable Opponent (the ever house-ruled) and now you can shift from &quot;meh, maybe he'll hit me&quot; to &quot;no, not a chance, ever, the end&quot; in a legend point. <br /> <br /> This does happen in other areas of the game, but quite frankly, it's most seen in combat for a number of reasons. It happens with the same math for the strong guy with no dex...sure.. he can hit like a brick, but he can't ever hit the guy that the dex monkey can hit 1/3 of the time. I've seen with mental/social things as well, although those tend to be more &quot;on/off&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think the important part here is that if you are going to have number of dice over a target number vs a static number of successes, you can't just have them work off the same scale (attribute + ability) without some kind of modification, and you have to be very aware of _any_ modifications to that scale. If they are going to have things to allow them to hit better, it should have an analog on defense that gives the same scale of bonus, with the note that defense against _everyone_ in a round is far better than attack against against any one target... you only get the bonus once on the attack, but you can get it on everyone on the defense.<br /> <br /> it's not that multiple dice are bad per se... you just have to constrain the numbers that can be had very strictly. After all, +1 die can give you upwards of 15% chance of success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T14:23:50-08:00","id":12959,"title":"","content":"I'll add in another post because the first is a little long.<br /> <br /> I might say that if you are going to have Defense be a static number (I think this is alright for the sake of not having to have an attack and a defense roll), the Defense should be more like the average of the Ability and the Attribute, or (if Abilities are constrained to a value less than the max of an Attribute), start off by halving the Attribute, or averaging it with another. But the range should _still_ be less than the expected number of dice that are being rolled against it.<br /> <br /> Consider Mr 9 Defense and Mr 4 Defense above. Mr 9 has 4 Dex, 3 Athletics, 2 Epic Dex. Mr 4 has 2 dex and 2 athletics. If one was to say Defense was (Dex + Athletics/2) + Epic dots, it's now<br /> <br /> Mr 6 Defense (Assuming round up) and Mr 2 Defense. More manageable, and one could use a 7 dice guy and not have quite as many issues.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind, these are just examples, so I don't know that that's actually the right choice. My feeling is though that a group of players should all have target numbers of successes within about 3 of each other, whether to hit or to damage or be hit or dominate someone or what.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T14:24:29-08:00","id":12962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/12818-scion-2e-mechanical-balance?p=12942#post12942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not as big of a cliff as you think, if you keep in mind the golden rule: <b>use enemies at multiple levels of difficulty.</b><br /> <br /> Almost every single fight should have at least two tiers of difficulty. One so your heavy weight combat characters can shine against, and one so your middle weight combat characters can shine against. Your light weights are probably not even involved in the combat, or are throwing around social/mental powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then this is obviously your major problem. The players must pick their battles, there is a time to fight and there is a time to flee. It sure will result in players that can't actively participate in battle, but if you are actively using Scion for its combat system, you are doing it wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T14:26:09-08:00","id":12964,"title":"","content":"Are you remembering that the STR tank can use STR as a to-hit people with grapples? If you add in factor, the DEX monkey may have some trouble in that the tank can hit him, and the very second he does the DEX Monkey basically goes crunch.<br /> <br /> I'll also say that one thing I think DnD 4e did right was using different abilities for AC calculation. In that you can use either Dexterity or Intelligence for your AC modifier. I don't think it'd be difficult to do something like that in Scion where you could say either the highest of your DEX or Wits is put into the DV formula*<br /> <br /> Assuming you're still using DV's, epics, and whatnot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":1183,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","user":"Sandact6","date":". 11-17-2013, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T14:29:13-08:00","id":12966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/12818-scion-2e-mechanical-balance?p=12942#post12942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not as big of a cliff as you think, if you keep in mind the golden rule: <b>use enemies at multiple levels of difficulty.</b><br /> <br /> Almost every single fight should have at least two tiers of difficulty. One so your heavy weight combat characters can shine against, and one so your middle weight combat characters can shine against. Your light weights are probably not even involved in the combat, or are throwing around social/mental powers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While I like that idea, the social/mental power route is less well developed in many ways. A lot more of &quot;spend a legend and impose a penalty on one guy for a round or two&quot;, where the heavy weights are getting &quot;spend no real resources and drop a guy completely&quot;. Dead is the best condition, as they say.<br /> <br /> also, the 33% mark (to toss out a number) for 4 successes and for 9 successes is a gap of about 10 dice <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That's pretty large.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T15:37:28-08:00","id":13005,"title":"","content":"The reason that social/mental powers aren't well developed is because they can be turned on PCs and players <i>hate</i> having control of their character taken away.<br /> <br /> &quot;You fall in love with Aphrodite because she uses Engender Love on you.&quot; &quot;I DO NOT! I CALL HER A HO AND PIMPSLAP HER!&quot;<br /> <br /> Yeah. Mental/social powers are just sticky because they affect the <i>player</i> more than the <i>character</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T16:24:35-08:00","id":13041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/12818-scion-2e-mechanical-balance?p=13005#post13005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason that social/mental powers aren't well developed is because they can be turned on PCs and players <i>hate</i> having control of their character taken away.<br /> <br /> &quot;You fall in love with Aphrodite because she uses Engender Love on you.&quot; &quot;I DO NOT! I CALL HER A HO AND PIMPSLAP HER!&quot;<br /> <br /> Yeah. Mental/social powers are just sticky because they affect the <i>player</i> more than the <i>character</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>A healthy separation of player and character is recommended. Players and Characters are distinct beings that are only connected by the game rules.<br /> <br /> But I agree, players should have a better control over their characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T16:48:59-08:00","id":13055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/12818-scion-2e-mechanical-balance?p=12964#post12964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you remembering that the STR tank can use STR as a to-hit people with grapples? If you add in factor, the DEX monkey may have some trouble in that the tank can hit him, and the very second he does the DEX Monkey basically goes crunch.<br /> <br /> I'll also say that one thing I think DnD 4e did right was using different abilities for AC calculation. In that you can use either Dexterity or Intelligence for your AC modifier. I don't think it'd be difficult to do something like that in Scion where you could say either the highest of your DEX or Wits is put into the DV formula*<br /> <br /> Assuming you're still using DV's, epics, and whatnot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, actually. that's what our brute ended up doing. But... quite frankly, kinda boring. No options because it was the only thing that worked with strength.<br /> <br /> and re: wits vs dex - ya, that's an option. one nWOD online does that actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T16:50:19-08:00","id":13056,"title":"","content":"Not disagreeing about social at all. The point remains, though - the options are bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T16:57:55-08:00","id":13062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Man in Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/12818-scion-2e-mechanical-balance?p=12962#post12962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then this is obviously your major problem. The players must pick their battles, there is a time to fight and there is a time to flee. It sure will result in players that can't actively participate in battle, but if you are actively using Scion for its combat system, you are doing it wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>with all due respect, that's a pretty poor argument in a system that has a solid 10% of the book dedicated to combat and is pretty much about heroes fighting a war across the earth and other planes of existence. It's a game about myths and heroes, and combat is simply a part of large portions of myths and heroes. <br /> <br /> and it's not like the math is magically in the combat system only. The point remains - once you have to overcome quite a few successes, and you can't do an extended success mechanic, it starts to break down pretty badly. The combat section just makes it painfully obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T17:42:28-08:00","id":13076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raleel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/12818-scion-2e-mechanical-balance?p=13062#post13062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">with all due respect, that's a pretty poor argument in a system that has a solid 10% of the book dedicated to combat and is pretty much about heroes fighting a war across the earth and other planes of existence. It's a game about myths and heroes, and combat is simply a part of large portions of myths and heroes.<br /> <br /> and it's not like the math is magically in the combat system only. The point remains - once you have to overcome quite a few successes, and you can't do an extended success mechanic, it starts to break down pretty badly. The combat section just makes it painfully obvious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately I must say that those 10% could have been better used elsewhere. And I already said that the system isn't perfect, his flaws lie mostly in its linearity and the absurd amount of automatic successes.<br /> <br /> Better could be a system where the player describes his action, gets X dice for it, roll for results and compares with the opposition, then the ST says what happens to them (and lets say, that character takes the difference in successes as penalty dice for his next action); when someone doesn't roll a single success he must leave the scene.<br /> <br /> &quot;I attack him with my mighty Guitar Axe, hitting the Frost Giant in the head before he has time to see it coming. A riff comes of the guitar, a sound full of headaches&quot; - says the player and gets 6 dice.<br /> &quot;The Giant tries to catch your guitar mid air.&quot; - says the ST and gains 4 dice.<br /> Both roll and the player wins by 1 success. &quot;The Giant fails to catch your guitar and the sound is amazing.&quot;, the Giant's next action gets -1 dice.<br /> ...<br /> When the Giant doesn't have any success, he either dies, flees, swears revenge and escapes.... he no longer has anything to say on this scene.<br /> <br /> Much simpler system, that maybe has a chance to do combat better. Just needs a table to guide the players and ST for the number of dice they get from their narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T20:18:42-08:00","id":13142,"title":"","content":"if I remember correctly, that's somewhat similar to how it was in oWOD. But it's been many years and I may be quite wrong. I would actually be pretty good with a simpler and perhaps somewhat less defined system. Is the production of Scion 2e constrained to Xd10 sort of systems? As for epics, I just don't think its reasonable to have the triangular scaling. It grossly distorts the possibilities. It makes heroes unable to trick gods and demigods, let alone directly confront them. It makes skills meaningless, and attributes, outside of requiring a minimum amount for epic levels, meaningless as well. I would say that +1 success for an epic dot is actually pretty strong under an Xd10 system. It's really equivalent to 2-4 dice you roll, based on the target number. A god with 10 in an epic stat is a tough customer, but probably even doable by a group of well motivated heroes with some good planning. It might also be a nice place to emphasize that whole &quot;if you don't have boons you're a chump&quot; aspect that is mentioned. Boons give you the edge to overcome epics that might be a bit over you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T21:13:37-08:00","id":13161,"title":"","content":"Personally, I have moved onto a <b>One Roll Resolution</b> system similar to what NWOD uses.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">COMBAT</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Scion 2.0 uses a single roll to resolve an attack. You use the most appropriate of your Strength or Dexterity for brawl or melee attacks, and the most appropriate of your Dexterity or Perception for marksmanship or thrown attacks. This result is compared against the Dodge DV or Soak DV of your targets (whichever is higher after all modifiers), and any successes above their DV are dealt as bashing, lethal, or aggravated damage.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">BONUSES AND PENALTIES</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Automatic successes from any source always add to the derived value associated with the Attribute or Ability in question, but bonus dice do not. If something gives you +2 successes to Dexterity then you would also gain +2 Dodge DV and Movement Speed.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Aggravated = \u00bd Soak DV.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Grappled = \u00bd Dodge DV.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Unexpected = \u00bd Dodge DV and Soak DV.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T00:15:04-08:00","id":13229,"title":"","content":"Iry, wheres that copyed from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1051-jsr","name":"JSR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T01:02:12-08:00","id":13243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JSR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/12818-scion-2e-mechanical-balance?p=13229#post13229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iry, wheres that copyed from?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's from a google document where we've basically complied all of the revisions we've made to Scion. Iry posted the mechanics but failed to mentioned that in response to this, we've had to balance other parts of the games in response; like dice-adders. Dice-adders were nerfed to hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T01:10:36-08:00","id":13251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Iry posted the mechanics but failed to mentioned that in response to this, we've had to balance other parts of the games in response; like dice-adders. Dice-adders were nerfed to hell.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Yes, honestly that is just one piece of a whole series of rebalances similar to what you have done for Gotham By Night. I went through and made several changes to what grants dice, and what grants successes. They work best when taken as a whole, but <b>One Roll Resolution</b> has worked very well in practice across many games.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T01:40:19-08:00","id":13264,"title":"","content":"Oooo....awesome. Because in the quote it says &quot;scion 2.0&quot; I thought it was an official leak from somewhere and I was confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1051-jsr","name":"JSR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T02:04:14-08:00","id":13277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JSR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/12818-scion-2e-mechanical-balance?p=13264#post13264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oooo....awesome. Because in the quote it says &quot;scion 2.0&quot; I thought it was an official leak from somewhere and I was confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>Naaah. I've been calling my houserules <b>&quot;Scion 2.0&quot;</b> long before the 2nd Edition of Scion was announced. It has no association with the upcoming edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T05:27:30-08:00","id":13341,"title":"","content":"Care to share a view link for the doc? I'd like to see and shop for our crew. We dearly dearly loved our scion game and would probably still be playing of we hadn't been interrupted by people having babies left and right (4 in our group in the last year)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T04:55:16-08:00","id":15311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raleel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/12818-scion-2e-mechanical-balance?p=13341#post13341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Care to share a view link for the doc? I'd like to see and shop for our crew. We dearly dearly loved our scion game and would probably still be playing of we hadn't been interrupted by people having babies left and right (4 in our group in the last year)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm happy to share some of it, but the Knacks and Boons section is under heavy construction right now. We're adding in Lesser and Greater Auras which are persistent effects, weaving in permanent cosmetic effects for certain boons to symbolize your growing connection to a purview, and adding more mythological connections. In any case, here is the core set of rules:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:36px\">Scion 2.0</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18IcvZDWbVVJ6yo58oY8zEYfAmOCMS1skw0saXzxgQQM/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...aXzxgQQM/edit#</a></div> </div> </div> </div> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T06:23:36-08:00","id":15332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/12818-scion-2e-mechanical-balance?p=15311#post15311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm happy to share some of it, but the Knacks and Boons section is under heavy construction right now. We're adding in Lesser and Greater Auras which are persistent effects, weaving in permanent cosmetic effects for certain boons to symbolize your growing connection to a purview, and adding more mythological connections. In any case, here is the core set of rules:</div> </div> </div> </div> Requested access this morning. Your permissions are locked down <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T07:52:05-08:00","id":15373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raleel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/12818-scion-2e-mechanical-balance?p=15332#post15332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Requested access this morning. Your permissions are locked down <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wonky. It is set for <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Public on the web - Anyone on the Internet can find and </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>view.</b></span></span></i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b> Added you regardless! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T09:08:58-08:00","id":15416,"title":"","content":"Thanks! very nice. I appreciate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T13:13:26-08:00","id":17265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/12818-scion-2e-mechanical-balance?p=15311#post15311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case, here is the core set of rules:</div> </div> </div> </div>Very cool!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T03:22:01-08:00","id":17639,"title":"","content":"I'm not up to date on this thread, and I'm not sure I want to spend the time to get up to date, but this little anecdote might prove useful.<br /> <br /> My friend was considering running a Scion game for our group and was unsure of the viability of it. Another friend (one with more experience as a ST) offered to run a brief canned adventure in order to show him what it was like. So the prospective ST made up a middling combat character with a good amount of magical oomph and I made up a buff tank Scion of... I forget. I decided I wanted to be properly buff so I asked if my character could have a coat that was made from the pelt of a Nemean Boar as armor. After all, the soak it gave me was less than what I already had so how bad could it be?<br /> <br /> Very bad, as it turned out, since in that adventure (a pre-made adventure set in WWII, not sure what it was called or where it was from) there was a very explicit line in it. It said &quot;Player character are supposed to go overland at this point. If they travel down the main road, they will not survive for the enemy forces are too numerous.&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, that was a load of bollocks, because my tank was perfectly capable of striding straight up to a tank, shrugging off direct hits from its main cannon and using his sword to lever off the top of the tank like the lid of a can and dicing up the soldiers inside like so much dried spinach. All while having the rest of the german army division emptying their machine guns at him on full auto coordinated fire. None of it mattered to him, he soaked it all and didn't take a single box of health damage without having to spend a single point of legend or willpower.<br /> <br /> Obviously, this is an extreme example, but when a character can be capable of this <i>at character creation</i>, obviously there is an issue.<br /> <br /> Again, not sure if this is relevant but I thought since this is a thread about Scien 2e mechanics, this might warrant attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1220-carnivalcash","name":"CarnivalCash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T03:51:44-08:00","id":17644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CarnivalCash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/12818-scion-2e-mechanical-balance?p=17639#post17639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously, this is an extreme example, but when a character can be capable of this <i>at character creation</i>, obviously there is an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've gone around and around the Nemean Hide issue back on the old forums. I continue to stand by the idea that access to Nemean Hide should probably be restricted until the band reaches Legend 5 as a general rule of thumb (dramatic and appropriate exceptions can always be made). Either that or a complete restructure of the way the 2nd Edition handles armor.<br /> <br /> Also, there was probably a lot your Storyteller could have done to challenge your tanky character if he so desired. It sounds like a lack of experience with the system more than anything else. It is probably a reasonable concern that those options are not immediately apparent, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T03:53:13-08:00","id":19075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/12818-scion-2e-mechanical-balance?p=17644#post17644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've gone around and around the Nemean Hide issue back on the old forums. I continue to stand by the idea that access to Nemean Hide should probably be restricted until the band reaches Legend 5 as a general rule of thumb (dramatic and appropriate exceptions can always be made). Either that or a complete restructure of the way the 2nd Edition handles armor.<br /> <br /> Also, there was probably a lot your Storyteller could have done to challenge your tanky character if he so desired. It sounds like a lack of experience with the system more than anything else. It is probably a reasonable concern that those options are not immediately apparent, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Running a canned adventure is, in my experience, the result of one of two things: organization module role-play (like Shadowrun Missions or RPGA campaigns) or lack of preparation/experience in managing the system in question.<br /> <br /> But yes, White Wolf's properties have a long and storied history of introducing elements that can destroy the core themes of their own games from character generation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T16:14:34-08:00","id":20845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/12818-scion-2e-mechanical-balance?p=19075#post19075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Running a canned adventure is, in my experience, the result of one of two things: organization module role-play (like Shadowrun Missions or RPGA campaigns) or lack of preparation/experience in managing the system in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's always my excuse, which is simple laziness. That said, even then, you've got to be careful which ones you use. There are no shortage of premade adventures that rather drastically suffer from a lack of advice in instances of Players slipping away from the railtracks.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}